{"module":"evidence","voice":"male","duration":272.1,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Is racism over? What the evidence shows today","start":0.0,"end":3.73,"words":[[0.05,0.22],[0.22,0.9],[0.9,1.33],[1.76,2.01],[2.01,2.19],[2.19,2.78],[2.78,3.12],[3.12,3.55]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Real progress has been made: the laws that named race are gone, and attitudes have changed.","start":4.53,"end":11.31,"words":[[4.58,4.9],[4.9,5.56],[5.56,5.81],[5.81,6.05],[6.05,6.46],[6.75,6.92],[6.92,7.16],[7.16,7.41],[7.41,7.82],[7.82,8.15],[8.15,8.23],[8.23,8.56],[8.84,9.09],[9.09,9.75],[9.75,9.99],[9.99,10.73]]},{"el":"intro","text":"But when researchers test whether people are still treated differently because of race, holding everything else equal, the answer keeps coming back yes.","start":11.66,"end":21.08,"words":[[11.7,11.94],[11.94,12.18],[12.18,12.81],[12.81,13.13],[13.13,13.45],[13.45,13.85],[13.85,13.93],[13.93,14.25],[14.25,14.73],[14.73,15.45],[15.45,15.85],[15.85,16.01],[16.01,16.41],[16.69,17.24],[17.24,17.8],[17.8,18.04],[18.04,18.52],[18.8,18.96],[18.96,19.28],[19.28,19.6],[19.6,20.0],[20.0,20.24],[20.24,20.56]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Housing","start":21.43,"end":22.17,"words":[[21.47,21.97]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In a 2012 national study for HUD, trained testers who differed only by race contacted landlords and agents; Black homebuyers were told about and shown roughly 17–18% fewer homes than equally qualified white buyers.","start":22.87,"end":38.71,"words":[[22.93,23.08],[23.08,23.24],[23.24,24.09],[24.09,24.64],[24.64,25.03],[25.03,25.19],[25.19,25.5],[25.77,26.24],[26.24,26.7],[26.7,26.86],[26.86,27.25],[27.25,27.64],[27.64,27.87],[27.87,28.19],[28.19,28.89],[28.89,29.51],[29.51,29.74],[29.74,30.45],[30.72,31.03],[31.03,31.73],[31.73,31.89],[31.89,32.28],[32.28,32.67],[32.67,32.9],[32.9,33.21],[33.21,33.6],[33.6,35.24],[35.24,35.55],[35.55,35.94],[35.94,36.17],[36.17,36.64],[36.64,37.34],[37.34,37.65],[37.65,38.12]]},{"el":"s0","text":"A 2019 Newsday undercover investigation on Long Island found Black testers were treated unequally in 49% of tests.","start":39.06,"end":47.7,"words":[[39.11,39.26],[39.26,40.23],[40.23,40.75],[40.75,41.35],[41.35,42.31],[42.31,42.46],[42.46,42.68],[42.68,43.13],[43.13,43.5],[43.5,43.8],[43.8,44.25],[44.25,44.4],[44.4,44.84],[44.84,45.44],[45.44,45.59],[45.59,46.63],[46.63,46.78],[46.78,47.22]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Lending and appraisals","start":48.6,"end":50.51,"words":[[48.64,49.2],[49.2,49.48],[49.48,50.33]]},{"el":"s1","text":"A study of millions of mortgages (Bartlett et al., 2022) found Black and Latino borrowers paid higher interest rates than comparable white borrowers, including with algorithmic lenders.","start":51.21,"end":64.51,"words":[[51.26,51.41],[51.41,51.81],[51.81,51.96],[51.96,52.52],[52.52,52.67],[52.67,53.31],[53.31,53.78],[53.78,53.94],[53.94,54.17],[54.45,55.55],[55.83,56.22],[56.22,56.54],[56.54,56.77],[56.77,57.33],[57.33,57.88],[57.88,58.19],[58.19,58.51],[58.51,59.06],[59.06,59.46],[59.46,59.69],[59.69,60.48],[60.48,60.8],[60.8,61.43],[61.7,62.33],[62.33,62.57],[62.57,63.36],[63.36,63.91]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Homes in majority-Black neighborhoods are valued about $48,000 less than similar homes elsewhere (Brookings, 2018).","start":64.86,"end":73.02,"words":[[64.91,65.27],[65.27,65.41],[65.41,66.34],[66.34,66.98],[66.98,67.05],[67.05,67.48],[67.48,67.83],[67.83,69.19],[69.19,69.4],[69.4,69.62],[69.62,70.04],[70.04,70.4],[70.4,70.83],[70.83,71.4],[71.65,72.58]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In 2020 a Black couple in Marin City, California, had their home appraised about $500,000 higher after removing family photos and having a white friend pose as the owner; their lawsuit settled in 2023.","start":73.37,"end":89.07,"words":[[73.41,73.57],[73.57,74.5],[74.5,74.65],[74.65,74.97],[74.97,75.35],[75.35,75.51],[75.51,75.9],[75.9,76.29],[76.56,77.33],[77.61,77.84],[77.84,78.07],[78.07,78.38],[78.38,78.93],[78.93,79.31],[79.31,81.02],[81.02,81.33],[81.33,81.64],[81.64,82.19],[82.19,82.65],[82.65,83.2],[83.2,83.43],[83.43,83.82],[83.82,83.97],[83.97,84.28],[84.28,84.67],[84.67,84.98],[84.98,85.14],[85.14,85.29],[85.29,85.68],[85.95,86.19],[86.19,86.57],[86.57,87.04],[87.04,87.2],[87.2,88.44]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Policing and courts","start":89.97,"end":91.66,"words":[[90.02,90.75],[90.75,91.07],[91.07,91.49]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The Stanford Open Policing Project analyzed nearly 100 million traffic stops (2020): Black drivers were stopped more often, the share of Black drivers stopped fell after dark when race is harder to see, and Black and Hispanic drivers were searched on less evidence.","start":92.36,"end":112.09,"words":[[92.41,92.59],[92.59,93.22],[93.22,93.67],[93.67,94.29],[94.29,95.01],[95.01,95.72],[95.72,96.17],[96.17,97.06],[97.06,97.6],[97.6,98.14],[98.14,98.58],[98.58,99.75],[100.06,100.42],[100.42,101.04],[101.04,101.22],[101.22,101.67],[101.67,101.85],[101.85,102.29],[102.61,102.79],[102.79,103.05],[103.05,103.23],[103.23,103.59],[103.59,104.22],[104.22,104.66],[104.66,104.93],[104.93,105.29],[105.29,105.56],[105.56,105.82],[105.82,106.18],[106.18,106.36],[106.36,106.72],[106.72,106.9],[106.9,107.17],[107.48,107.75],[107.75,108.1],[108.1,108.37],[108.37,109.09],[109.09,109.71],[109.71,109.89],[109.89,110.34],[110.34,110.52],[110.52,110.79],[110.79,111.5]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The U.S. Sentencing Commission found in 2017 that Black men received federal sentences about 19% longer than similar white men.","start":112.44,"end":122.52,"words":[[112.49,112.65],[112.65,113.04],[113.43,114.13],[114.13,114.68],[114.68,115.07],[115.07,115.22],[115.22,116.31],[116.31,116.55],[116.55,116.86],[116.86,117.1],[117.1,117.56],[117.56,118.11],[118.11,118.81],[118.81,119.2],[119.2,120.22],[120.22,120.61],[120.61,120.84],[120.84,121.31],[121.31,121.62],[121.62,121.94]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In Flowers v. Mississippi (2019) the Supreme Court overturned a conviction after a prosecutor struck 41 of 42 Black prospective jurors over six trials.","start":122.87,"end":134.64,"words":[[122.92,123.07],[123.07,123.53],[123.53,123.76],[124.15,124.77],[124.77,125.77],[126.04,126.19],[126.19,126.66],[126.66,126.89],[126.89,127.5],[127.5,127.66],[127.66,128.35],[128.35,128.66],[128.66,128.81],[128.81,129.58],[129.58,129.97],[129.97,130.51],[130.51,130.66],[130.66,131.13],[131.13,131.43],[131.43,132.2],[132.2,132.82],[132.82,133.13],[133.13,133.44],[133.44,134.05]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Medicine and algorithms","start":135.54,"end":137.54,"words":[[135.59,136.14],[136.14,136.42],[136.42,137.35]]},{"el":"s3","text":"A 2019 study in Science found that a widely used algorithm for deciding which patients get extra care underestimated how sick Black patients were, because it used past health spending as a stand-in for need.","start":138.24,"end":153.56,"words":[[138.29,138.45],[138.45,139.55],[139.55,139.97],[139.97,140.14],[140.14,140.65],[140.65,141.07],[141.07,141.32],[141.32,141.49],[141.49,141.99],[141.99,142.33],[142.33,143.09],[143.09,143.26],[143.26,143.93],[143.93,144.27],[144.27,144.94],[144.94,145.2],[145.2,145.7],[145.7,145.96],[145.96,147.22],[147.22,147.47],[147.47,147.73],[147.73,148.06],[148.06,148.74],[148.74,148.99],[149.29,149.71],[149.71,149.88],[149.88,150.21],[150.21,150.55],[150.55,150.89],[150.89,151.48],[151.48,151.65],[151.65,151.81],[151.81,152.4],[152.4,152.57],[152.57,152.91]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Fixing it would more than double the number of Black patients flagged for help.","start":153.91,"end":158.15,"words":[[153.95,154.37],[154.37,154.5],[154.5,154.71],[154.71,154.85],[154.85,155.06],[155.06,155.4],[155.4,155.54],[155.54,155.88],[155.88,156.02],[156.02,156.3],[156.3,156.85],[156.85,157.19],[157.19,157.33],[157.33,157.68]]},{"el":"s3","text":"(See also “Health” on pain and pulse oximeters.)","start":158.5,"end":162.13,"words":[[158.54,158.72],[158.72,159.17],[159.17,159.54],[159.54,159.72],[159.72,160.08],[160.08,160.35],[160.35,160.72],[160.72,161.62]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Children and families","start":163.03,"end":164.53,"words":[[163.07,163.62],[163.62,163.83],[163.83,164.31]]},{"el":"s4","text":"A 2017 study estimated that more than half of Black children (53%) experience a child-protective-services investigation by age 18, compared with 37% of all children.","start":165.23,"end":179.07,"words":[[165.27,165.42],[165.42,166.47],[166.47,166.84],[166.84,167.59],[167.59,167.81],[167.81,167.96],[167.96,168.18],[168.18,168.41],[168.41,168.56],[168.56,168.85],[168.85,169.45],[169.45,170.5],[170.76,171.65],[171.65,171.8],[171.8,173.45],[173.45,174.42],[174.42,174.64],[174.64,174.94],[174.94,175.39],[175.65,176.17],[176.17,176.4],[176.4,177.52],[177.52,177.66],[177.66,177.81],[177.81,178.49]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Black students are suspended at much higher rates than white students for similar behavior, according to federal civil rights data.","start":179.42,"end":188.37,"words":[[179.46,179.78],[179.78,180.49],[180.49,180.57],[180.57,181.28],[181.28,181.44],[181.44,181.76],[181.76,182.08],[182.08,182.48],[182.48,182.71],[182.71,183.03],[183.03,183.75],[183.75,183.9],[183.9,184.38],[184.38,185.09],[185.37,185.85],[185.85,186.01],[186.01,186.56],[186.56,186.96],[186.96,187.36],[187.36,187.83]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Everyday life","start":189.27,"end":190.35,"words":[[189.32,189.9],[189.9,190.23]]},{"el":"s5","text":"On Airbnb, guests with distinctively Black names were about 16% less likely to be accepted than identical guests with white-sounding names (2017).","start":191.05,"end":201.89,"words":[[191.1,191.25],[191.25,191.71],[191.98,192.37],[192.37,192.6],[192.6,193.52],[193.52,193.83],[193.83,194.21],[194.21,194.36],[194.36,194.75],[194.75,195.75],[195.75,195.98],[195.98,196.44],[196.44,196.59],[196.59,196.74],[196.74,197.36],[197.36,197.59],[197.59,198.36],[198.36,198.74],[198.74,198.97],[198.97,199.82],[199.82,200.2],[200.2,201.35]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Anti-Black bias is the most common motive in hate crimes reported to the FBI every year.","start":202.24,"end":208.35,"words":[[202.28,202.9],[202.9,203.29],[203.29,203.44],[203.44,203.59],[203.59,203.98],[203.98,204.36],[204.36,204.83],[204.83,204.98],[204.98,205.29],[205.29,205.75],[205.75,206.29],[206.29,206.45],[206.45,206.6],[206.6,207.14],[207.14,207.45],[207.45,207.76]]},{"el":"s5","text":"And this site's own data shows how rarely “suspicious person” 911 calls find a crime.","start":208.7,"end":214.87,"words":[[208.74,208.95],[208.95,209.16],[209.16,209.5],[209.5,209.71],[209.71,210.06],[210.06,210.34],[210.34,210.54],[210.54,210.89],[210.89,211.45],[211.45,211.79],[211.79,213.11],[213.11,213.39],[213.39,213.74],[213.74,213.87],[213.87,214.29]]},{"el":"h6","text":"Talking with someone who thinks racism is over","start":215.77,"end":218.51,"words":[[215.79,216.15],[216.15,216.36],[216.36,216.79],[216.79,216.94],[216.94,217.29],[217.29,217.87],[217.87,218.01],[218.01,218.3]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Agree on what's true.","start":219.21,"end":220.87,"words":[[219.26,219.56],[219.56,219.71],[219.71,220.02],[220.02,220.32]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Much has changed; say so.","start":221.22,"end":223.45,"words":[[221.27,221.52],[221.52,221.72],[221.72,222.29],[222.52,222.71],[222.71,222.97]]},{"el":"s6","text":"The question isn't whether things are better, but whether people are still treated differently.","start":223.8,"end":228.38,"words":[[223.85,223.97],[223.97,224.46],[224.46,224.77],[224.77,225.01],[225.01,225.26],[225.26,225.32],[225.32,225.63],[225.84,226.03],[226.03,226.27],[226.27,226.58],[226.58,226.64],[226.64,226.89],[226.89,227.25],[227.25,227.87]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Lead with experiments, not anecdotes.","start":228.73,"end":231.84,"words":[[228.76,228.98],[228.98,229.2],[229.2,230.16],[230.41,230.63],[230.63,231.37]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Audit studies change only race.","start":232.19,"end":234.71,"words":[[232.24,232.53],[232.53,232.95],[232.95,233.45],[233.45,233.8],[233.8,234.15]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Ask: “If the résumés were identical, what explains the difference?”","start":235.06,"end":239.39,"words":[[235.11,235.37],[235.6,235.72],[235.72,235.85],[235.85,236.37],[236.37,236.5],[236.5,237.21],[237.43,237.63],[237.63,238.21],[238.21,238.33],[238.33,238.85]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Invite them to check.","start":239.74,"end":241.19,"words":[[239.79,240.17],[240.17,240.36],[240.36,240.49],[240.49,240.8]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Every claim here is labeled and sourced.","start":241.54,"end":244.83,"words":[[241.59,241.96],[241.96,242.42],[242.42,242.69],[242.69,242.88],[242.88,243.52],[243.52,243.79],[243.79,244.25]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Skepticism is fine; apply it to the evidence.","start":245.18,"end":248.6,"words":[[245.22,246.0],[246.0,246.14],[246.14,246.49],[246.74,247.09],[247.09,247.23],[247.23,247.37],[247.37,247.51],[247.51,248.08]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Share a story, with permission.","start":248.95,"end":251.78,"words":[[249.0,249.26],[249.26,249.44],[249.44,249.95],[250.26,250.52],[250.52,251.21]]},{"el":"s6","text":"One person they know matters more than a statistic.","start":252.13,"end":255.46,"words":[[252.18,252.41],[252.41,252.8],[252.8,253.03],[253.03,253.27],[253.27,253.66],[253.66,253.82],[253.82,254.05],[254.05,254.21],[254.21,254.99]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Don't shame.","start":255.81,"end":257.36,"words":[[255.9,256.29],[256.29,256.68]]},{"el":"s6","text":"People defend themselves when they feel accused.","start":257.71,"end":260.55,"words":[[257.74,258.08],[258.08,258.48],[258.48,259.01],[259.01,259.21],[259.21,259.41],[259.41,259.61],[259.61,260.07]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Talk about systems, not their character.","start":260.9,"end":264.18,"words":[[260.9,261.14],[261.14,261.54],[261.54,262.18],[262.46,262.7],[262.7,262.94],[262.94,263.59]]},{"el":"s6","text":"Give them something to do.","start":264.53,"end":266.23,"words":[[264.63,264.83],[264.83,265.03],[265.03,265.44],[265.44,265.57],[265.57,265.77]]},{"el":"s6","text":"A small action, like reading one module, keeps the door open.","start":266.58,"end":271.22,"words":[[266.63,266.78],[266.78,267.09],[267.09,267.56],[267.83,268.14],[268.14,268.53],[268.53,268.76],[268.76,269.31],[269.58,269.89],[269.89,270.05],[270.05,270.2],[270.2,270.67]]}]}